Applied a driver's declared defaults when a provider is created. Every driver already describes a sensible value for the settings that have one — GitHub's `read:user user:email` scope, the random userid source, link-by-email off — and the schema carrying them is what `@identity-drivers` serves. Nothing applied them: a provider created without a scope stored no scope at all, so its first sign-in asked GitHub for no permissions and came back without the email address it needed.

`ProviderConfig` now fills in every setting the caller did not supply, from the schema its own driver declares. A key that is present wins whether or not it is empty, because clearing a setting is a decision rather than a gap; a provider whose driver has been removed is left exactly as it was stored, there being no schema left to consult. @ericof
